  "description": "<p>Janna Wemekamp reports:</p>\n\n<p>Fedora's search functions fail with the following error if the pid column isn't requested as part of the result set:</p>\n\n<p>    javax.ws.rs.WebApplicationException: fedora.server.errors.StorageDeviceException: Error with sql database. The column name pid was not found in this ResultSet.</p>\n\n<p>This is true of the 'search' web interface and the REST API.</p>\n\n<p>Eg.<br/>\n<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects?title=true&amp;identifier=true&amp;terms=&amp;query=pid~demo%3A*&amp;maxResults=20\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects?title=true&amp;identifier=true&amp;terms=&amp;query=pid~demo%3A*&amp;maxResults=20</a><br/>\n<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/search?title=true&amp;identifier=true&amp;terms=&amp;query=pid~demo%3A*&amp;maxResults=20\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/search?title=true&amp;identifier=true&amp;terms=&amp;query=pid~demo%3A*&amp;maxResults=20</a></p>",
